    "result": "Perfect! The fix has been successfully applied and compiled. Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary of the Fix\n\n**Problem:** `frai gate init --ci` did not create the GitHub Actions workflow file, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked.\n\n**Root Cause:** The action handler for the `gate` command in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was incorrectly receiving parameters from Commander.js. The first parameter was the Command object (not the variadic arguments array), so the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the action handler (lines 742-755) to:\n1. Accept all parameters using rest parameters: `async (...allParams: any[])`\n2. Extract the Command object from the last parameter: `const command = allParams[allParams.length - 1]`\n3. Get the actual variadic arguments: `const args = command?.args ?? []`\n4. Pass the correct arguments to spawnSync: `spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...args], ...)`\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- \u2705 Fixed `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-755)\n- \u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Verified the compiled output contains the fix\n\nThe fix ensures that when users run `frai gate init --ci`, the complete argument list `['init', '--ci']` is passed to the frai-gate CLI, allowing it to correctly recognize the `--ci` flag and create the GitHub Actions workflow file at `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.",
